{"date": "2026-10-11", "rank": 3, "topic": "住房", "title": "Rent-a-Room Tax Limit Rises to 16,000 Euro", "level": "B2", "summaryZh": "房間出租免稅上限從一萬四調高到一萬六歐元，盼增加學生床位。", "sources": [{"name": "The Irish Times", "url": "https://www.irishtimes.com/ireland/2026/10/11/will-rent-a-room-scheme-increase-encourage-more-landlords-to-participate/"}], "paragraphs": ["People in Ireland who rent out a room in their own home will soon be able to earn more money without paying tax on it. In Budget 2027, the Government raised the tax-free limit of the rent-a-room scheme from 14,000 euro to 16,000 euro a year. It is the first increase since 2017.", "The scheme has become much more popular in recent years. The number of people claiming the relief almost doubled between 2020 and 2024, rising from about 9,300 to more than 18,000. Universities say the number of rooms offered to students in family homes has also grown, from around 2,000 in 2022 to over 5,000 this year.", "However, there is an important rule to remember. If a homeowner earns even slightly more than the limit, all of the rental income becomes taxable, not just the extra amount.", "Ministers argue that the change will make more beds available quickly, without any need for planning permission or new construction. The scheme will now also cover small cabins built in a homeowner's garden, although this part of the plan has been strongly criticised by opposition politicians."], "gloss": {"a": {"zh": "一個", "pos": "art.", "base": "a"}, "able": {"zh": "能夠（be able to）", "pos": "adj.", "base": "able"}, "about": {"zh": "大約", "pos": "adv.", "base": "about"}, "all": {"zh": "全部；都", "pos": "det.", "base": "all"}, "almost": {"zh": "幾乎", "pos": "adv.", "base": "almost"}, "also": {"zh": "也", "pos": "adv.", "base": "also"}, "although": {"zh": "雖然；儘管", "pos": "conj.", "base": "although"}, "amount": {"zh": "數額；金額", "pos": "n.", "base": "amount"}, "an": {"zh": "一個", "pos": "art.", "base": "an"}, "and": {"zh": "和；而且", "pos": "conj.", "base": "and"}, "